# Keep the Docker build context small: the image holds only the pinned
# environment. Code + data (including the large/restricted inputs) are MOUNTED
# at run time, not copied into the image. See docker/DOCKER_GUIDE.md.
#
# This is a DENYLIST, so a directory not named here IS sent to the Docker daemon
# as build context. Every large tree in the package must therefore appear below;
# if you add one, add it here too. Without the simulated-payload and model
# entries, `docker build -f docker/Dockerfile .` streams tens of gigabytes into
# the daemon before the first instruction runs.
data/
synthetic_pipeline/
output/
output-simulated/
models/
manual_figures/
code/
r_scripts/
paper/
docs/
certification/
.github/
*.zip
*.sha256
.DS_Store
**/__pycache__/
**/.ipynb_checkpoints/
.git/
.Rhistory
.RData
# The Dockerfile explicitly COPYs the few files it needs:
#   requirements-lock.txt, docker/renv.lock, docker/install_r_packages.R,
#   docker/entrypoint.sh
!requirements-lock.txt
!docker/
